docs/product/prd.md:3:**v0.6 · 2026-09-28 · macOS/Windows Electron desktop · review required**
docs/product/prd.md:5:This version preserves approved PRD scope and records the user's explicit selection of Electron for the installed macOS and Windows desktop app with an app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar. Electron is a product decision, not evidence of packaged compatibility or runtime security. F-01–18, exclusions, and integrated scenarios remain unchanged. Earlier reviews are historical evidence; these amendments require fresh product and design-spec review. Text changes are not app implementation or verification.
docs/product/prd.md:13:배포 형태는 **macOS와 Windows용 Electron 설치형 로컬 데스크톱 앱**이다. Electron main process가 창과 앱 소유 OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar의 수명을 관리하며, renderer에는 임의 로컬 경로·셸·프로세스 권한이나 sidecar credential을 주지 않는다. Electron 선택은 SDK/서버 호환성, 플랫폼 패키징 또는 런타임 보안을 입증하지 않는다. 로컬 앱은 완전 오프라인을 뜻하지 않으며 기존 설정의 원격 모델·MCP를 사용할 수 있다. 개인용 unsigned 빌드는 범위에 포함하며 public distribution, store, signing/notarization, auto-update service는 별도 범위다.
docs/product/prd.md:89:| 실행 엔진 | 앱이 소유하는 OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar에 버전이 맞는 `@opencode/client`로 연결한다. 셸은 비교 후 사용자가 Electron을 선택했다(ADR-0002). 정확한 패키지 호환성과 플랫폼 런타임은 아직 검증하지 않았다. 기존 `@opencode-ai/sdk`의 `/v2`로 조용히 되돌리지 않는다. |
docs/product/prd.md:97:| 운영·패키징 | 설치형 macOS/Windows 앱의 선택된 shell과 sidecar 시작/종료 책임, 알림·자동화 지속 조건, 데이터 위치·보존·마이그레이션을 확정한다. 창/업데이트/서명 요구사항은 사용자가 선택한 shell에 맞춰 승인된 플랫폼 스펙으로 구체화한다. |
docs/product/prd.md:137:PRD v0.6 records the user's explicit Electron selection for the installed macOS and Windows desktop app with an app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar. F-01–18 behavior and exclusions remain unchanged. Current independent product/design-spec reviews and approval of the exact integrated document set are still required before implementation. Figma connection is user-reported, not evidence that a file or design system was inspected. No public release action is implied.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:31:Illustrative renderer ownership: `pages/workbench` composes route context; `widgets/session-workspace` joins the transcript, tool activity, and sidebar; `features/send-message`, `features/decide-permission`, and `features/interrupt-run` own user intents; `entities/session`, `entities/run`, and `entities/permission` own identifiers, read models, and display mapping; `shared` owns bridge client, safe formatting, and cross-domain utilities. A widget may compose features without taking authority for their bridge mutations. This is an initial graph, not a requirement to create empty folders. Create a slice when it has a distinct public API and independent use or change pressure; split a package when independent build/release cadence, incompatible runtime dependencies, or repeated boundary violations are measured. Avoid a generic `core` package before that evidence.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:33:Nx tasks will be `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, and `build` only where a project has a real command. Define named inputs from tracked source, lockfile, tool config, and token source; define outputs for generated CSS and build artifacts. Do not cache `serve`, SDK host probes, migrations, permission decisions, workspace-mutating commands, or live/stateful E2E. Use **local cache only** initially; no Nx Cloud, remote service, or subscription. Cache hits are performance evidence, not test execution evidence. Untrusted imported project content must not enter the app's build configuration or local task cache; see [Nx cache security](https://nx.dev/docs/kb/cache-security). A build task should operate on reviewed source, with an isolated temporary fixture for adversarial project tests. Measure cold/warm task duration and cache correctness before adding distributed caching or more task orchestration. Nx and `@nx/vite` must be the same version, per the [Nx Vite integration](https://nx.dev/docs/technologies/build-tools/vite/introduction); exact package peers are a bootstrap check.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:37:Choose **React with Vite for the browser renderer**. The product is a local app whose trusted execution and API live in a separate bridge; it has no public SEO or server-rendering requirement. Vite gives a direct static renderer build and browser development loop without adding Next.js server/routing authority beside the bridge. Current Vite documentation describes its [Rolldown/Oxc architecture](https://vite.dev/guide/why.html); do not assume the old esbuild/Rollup implementation when tuning plugins or tests. Use a small route layer within React; choose a routing package only when navigation and URL semantics demand it. Durable router, history, query-string and persisted navigation state may carry a validated project/workspace/session **ID** and non-sensitive view state, never canonical paths, raw prompts, bootstrap secrets, approval receipts, or permission authority. Any transient one-time launcher-fragment bootstrap remains a candidate governed exclusively by the unchanged execution contract section 5: exchange and remove it immediately, and pass its history/referrer/log/preview leak checks before adoption. This is not ordinary navigation state or an authorization exception. Bridge lookup and authorization determine what an ID can open.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:45:The bridge is the authority for all operations, permissions, policy revisions, session/run effects, process lifetime, and durable records. The renderer keeps projections, drafts, and navigation state. Assign each value one owner:
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:49:| Persisted metadata and ordinary read models | Bridge/SQLite; `TanStack Query` caches non-live project/workspace/session metadata and ordinary reads | Query data is a disposable view, keyed by install epoch/project/workspace/session. Exclude live transcript, run status, pending permission and effective-policy fields owned by the event projection. Never make a cache hit proof of an effect. |
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:56:This separation follows [TanStack Query defaults](https://tanstack.com/query/latest/docs/framework/react/guides/important-defaults), [Zustand scoped stores](https://zustand.docs.pmnd.rs/learn/guides/initialize-state-with-props), and [React reducer/Context guidance](https://react.dev/learn/scaling-up-with-reducer-and-context). Configure read queries' stale time and mount/focus/reconnect refetch for local bridge behavior deliberately; default stale-on-arrival and three failed-query retries are not a product policy. A bounded retry is acceptable for idempotent reads, with source-health display. Mutations use **retry 0**. The client sends the bridge-required idempotency key and expected revision; only the bridge may reconcile an uncertain effect, and the UI distinguishes `accepted`, `applied`, `effect_confirmed`, and `unknown`. Do not persist Query caches, Zustand permission state, tokens, approval decisions, or optimistic effect claims. Persist only bridge-owned records and intentionally saved user drafts under the existing retention contract.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:58:The app-owned event adapter keys data by install epoch, project, workspace, session, and run. It subscribes first, captures the last durable app cursor, reads `GET /snapshot`, replays `GET /events?after=`, de-duplicates by event ID/sequence, and compares revisions and source health. A duplicate or lower revision cannot roll state backward. The adapter batches high-frequency token deltas for rendering while applying identity, status, and permission changes promptly; an initial target is at most one visible transcript commit per animation frame, with a measured backlog/latency threshold before tuning. A gap is shown as `history_gap`; no invented transcript fills it. A disconnect marks live state stale, disables stale tool/permission actions, and triggers re-subscribe and reconciliation. Keep session-scoped draft, approval, and pending action maps separate so tab switches cannot leak actions between sessions. Assistant-ui consumes this projection through its external runtime; Tool UI renders only schema-validated tool results dispatched from that same runtime. Unknown tools use the safe generic card. A card action carries original session/request/policy identifiers back to the bridge for fresh validation. This preserves the approved [assistant-ui / Tool UI division](../design/specs/workbench-ux.md#assistant-ui와-tool-ui의-경계).
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:60:The event adapter fetches its reconciliation snapshot directly through the transport; it does not retain a second live snapshot in Query. Metadata invalidation may notify Query, but live fields remain exclusively in the external projection. Components select from that owner and never copy authoritative fields into a local UI store. Abort in-flight reads and discard callbacks from a prior scope/epoch during teardown. The transcript projection releases listeners and buffers when its owning session scope is disposed, while the bridge retains actual execution lifetime.
docs/decisions/0001-workbench-platform.md:84:3. **State:** use synthetic event sequences for duplicate/out-of-order events, lower revisions, session switch isolation, disconnect/reconnect with gaps, batch latency, and stale approval. Verify Query refetch cannot report a mutation success, mutation retry is zero, and bridge revisions/receipts are the only effect authority. Live SDK event behavior remains a separate S-01/S-09 gate.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:3:**v0.6 · 2026-09-28 · Electron app-owned sidecar · independent review required**
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:5:이 문서는 [PRD v0.6 Electron desktop amendment](../product/prd.md)의 F-01~18을 구현하기 위한 앱 소유 계약이다. [desktop bootstrap 계획 revision 18과 계약](../workplans/desktop-app-bootstrap/plan.md)이 이 증분 작업의 순서와 승인 상태를 정의한다. 과거 domain-specs 계획은 역사적 입력이며 현재 승인 근거가 아니다. [UX 명세](../design/specs/workbench-ux.md)는 사용자에게 보이는 상태·조작의 기준이며, 여기서는 그 상태를 확정할 실행 근거를 정한다. 아래 `PROPOSED`는 앱이 만들어야 할 계약이지 OpenCode API의 존재나 실행 검증을 뜻하지 않는다. 패키지 설치, 런타임 호출, 보안 시험은 아직 수행하지 않았다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:11:| Electron main + preload | 앱 창, trusted local API/bridge, OS dialog/notification adapter, narrow host API admission, exact sidecar lifecycle | Main is the trusted local authority; renderer content is never trusted by origin alone; exact package/runtime enforcement remains to be verified |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:13:| Electron main local service modules | 요청 검증, 경로·권한 게이트, 실행 조정, 일지·복구, OpenCode client/adapter | 유일한 앱 실행 진입점. 자기 호출에도 같은 검증; no separate loopback service for desktop renderer |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:14:| App-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` child | SDK-supported sessions/tools/events and native runtime behavior | Electron main starts and owns the exact child; renderer and preview never receive its URL credential |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:15:| App operation modules | import, file/Git changes, direct tools, scheduler and explicit native gaps | Electron main admission and audit path; browser-only bridge is not desktop authority |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:18:Delivery target is an **installed Electron desktop app for macOS and Windows** with an app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar. The user selected Electron after the comparison recorded in ADR-0002. Electron main is the trusted local API/bridge, owns the window and exact sidecar lifecycle, and runs the version-matched client. The versioned, narrow preload API replaces browser HTTP origin pairing for desktop requests. Do not expose sidecar credentials to renderer-wide code or untrusted preview contents. The main process is the sole authority for files, Git, PTY, process, permissions, audit, and recovery. Keep the existing HTTP bridge only as a separate explicitly supported browser mode; it is not part of packaged desktop request routing. No cloud API, Supabase, account/RBAC, or external telemetry is added. Existing remote-model/MCP boundaries remain unchanged.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:20:OpenCode v2 runtime contract is an app-owned foreground `opencode serve` sidecar. Electron main connects only to its exact child using the version-matched [`@opencode/client`](https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/build/client/) API. Do not use the embedded SDK host or a shared-service helper because the user confirmed app-owned sidecar lifecycle. Main keeps server credentials private, verifies readiness and identity, and owns startup, shutdown, and reaping. The desktop UI calls typed main-process service modules through preload; it does not call an HTTP bridge directly. Pin the CLI and client versions together and check the experimental [HTTP API](https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/api) against the packaged server after the exact document set is approved. Electron is selected in ADR-0002; package compatibility remains unverified.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:30:| `sessions` | `sessionId`, `workspaceId`, `nativeSessionId?`, `parentSessionId?`, `title`, `archived`, `pinned`, `unreadCursor`, `draft`, `viewState` | 앱 메타데이터와 native session을 명시적으로 매핑 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:31:| `runs` | `runId`, `sessionId`, `caller`, `requestedConfig`, `effectiveConfig?`, `state`, `startedAt`, `endedAt?`, `nativeTurnRef?` | native 상태 조회가 실행 완료의 권위 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:35:| `policy_revisions` | `revision`, `sessionId`, `parentRevision?`, `rulesDigest`, `effectiveAt?`, `state` | 적용 확인된 revision만 effective |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:41:표시용 기록의 보존 만료와 재실행 방지 기록의 수명은 분리한다. 내용 원문을 지워도 아직 유효한 실행 namespace에서는 operation ID·입력 digest·최종/unknown 상태의 최소 tombstone을 유지한다. 이 최소 기록까지 지우려면 해당 session/workspace의 실행 namespace를 폐기하고 pending 요청·capability를 무효화한다. 폐기된 namespace의 옛 ID/키 요청은 새 작업으로 접수하지 않고 거절한다. 전체 앱 데이터 초기화는 실제 실행을 먼저 종료·대조하고 새 설치 epoch를 만든다. 다시 import하면 새 ID로 명시적 실행을 시작하며 과거 native 요청을 replay하지 않는다. tombstone은 사용자에게 삭제 범위와 함께 설명하고 원문이나 자격 증명을 담지 않는다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:47:API는 앱 소유 `/api/v1`이며 OpenCode 경로가 아니다. 모든 쓰기는 `requestId`(호출 상관관계), `Idempotency-Key`, `expectedRevision` 또는 `If-Match`를 받는다. 응답은 `{operationId, state, object, revision, evidenceRefs, error?}` 형식이다. `202`는 접수이며 성공이 아니다. side effect 완료는 검증 영수증과 조회 결과가 맞을 때만 `succeeded`다. 멱등 키는 로컬 호출 주체·session 또는 workspace 범위·operation 종류로 namespace를 나눈다. 동일 범위의 동일 키·동일 digest 재요청은 기존 operation을 돌려주고, 동일 키·다른 입력은 `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:51:| 경로 검토·등록·생성·제거 | `POST /paths/inspect`, `/projects/import`, `/workspaces`, `/workspaces/{id}/delete-check`, `/workspaces/{id}/delete`; `DELETE /projects/{id}/registration` | 경로 canonicalization, trust, 최종 identity·dirty 재검사 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:52:| 작업·대화·위임 | `/sessions`, `/sessions/{id}/runs`, `/runs/{id}/interrupt`, `/delegations`, `/delegations/{id}/interrupt` | native 매핑, 모델 입력, child scope, 실제 종료 확인 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:56:| 복구·기록·자동화 | `/snapshot`, `/events`, `/exports`, `/imports`, `/retention`, `/jobs`, `/jobs/{id}/pause` | 보존·redaction·권한·스케줄 상태 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:58:`GET /snapshot`은 DB 매핑, native session/worktree/pending request, bridge process registry를 조회해 `{snapshotRevision, sourceHealth, objects, gaps}`를 낸다. `GET /events?after=<seq>`는 앱이 영속화한 event만 재생한다. WebSocket/SSE는 live 알림이며 cursor 순서·중복 제거 뒤 snapshot과 대조한다. native 구독이 [live-only이며 자동 재생·재접속을 보장하지 않는다는 문서](https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/build/client/) 때문에 native 누락을 앱 event로 꾸며 채우지 않는다. 앱 일지 sequence에도 hole이 있거나 native 중단 기간이 있으면 `history_gap(from,to,reason)`을 영속화한다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:60:이벤트 envelope는 `{eventId, appSeq, type, objectType, objectId, projectId?, workspaceId?, sessionId?, runId?, childId?, nativeRef?, policyRevision?, operationId?, observedAt, payloadVersion, payload}`다. `accepted`, `started`, `approval_pending`, `effect_confirmed`, `interrupt_requested`, `terminated`, `failed`, `unknown`, `reconciled`는 다른 type이다. UI는 object ID로 분리된 projection을 만들고 active tab 전환으로 다른 세션의 draft/approval을 재사용하지 않는다. 앱 event는 관측 근거 링크를 제공하되 보안 강제의 증거 자체는 아니다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:64:Electron's main process is the trusted desktop host and owns the app window, the exact app-launched OpenCode v2 `serve` child, its readiness/authentication lifecycle, and the version-matched `@opencode/client` connection. It must never attach to a pre-existing ambient server. The renderer uses a closed, versioned schema through a narrow preload `contextBridge`; enable context isolation and renderer sandboxing, disable Node integration, and expose named functions only. No arbitrary channel, Node object, shell, filesystem, process API, or sidecar URL/credential crosses into renderer. Main validates sender, frame, lifecycle, and payload shape; unexpected navigation and child windows are denied by default. Preview content runs without the privileged preload or sidecar credential and uses a separate browsing context. Exact Electron, Chromium, server, and packager versions plus per-OS behavior remain unverified until the approved probes run.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:66:The renderer adapter is injected by the desktop bootstrap and has the same public app contract as the browser test adapter, but it does not inherit HTTP Origin/CORS pairing as its security proof. The selected host mediates messages to the app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` process. Preview is a separate untrusted surface with no privileged host API or sidecar capability; allowed navigation, local URL behavior, CSP and external open actions are checked independently. Dev mode and packaged mode are separate trust configurations. A failed sidecar start leaves the app in a visible unavailable state and exposes no fallback direct renderer-to-sidecar credential.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:74:| 프로젝트/경로 | `inspecting → connected|read_only|denied|missing`; `creating → created|created_setup_failed|failed`; `connected → deleted` | 파일 identity/Git 상태 조회 후 연결. `created_setup_failed`는 디렉터리 존재를 보존 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:75:| 세션 | `draft → queued → running → awaiting_approval|interrupt_requested|completed|failed|unknown`; `interrupt_requested → terminated|unknown` | native session/turn 재조회로 종료 판정. 접수만으로 완료 금지 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:96:**Browser-test-only scope:** the browser bridge's loopback/capability pairing, fragment bootstrap, tab-held authorization header, CSRF, `Origin`/`Host`, WebSocket upgrade, and request schema form a separate browser-mode proposal and do not authorize or define the Electron host contract. They require a separate reviewed browser security mode before use. Electron desktop mode uses main's typed preload API and in-process service modules; the renderer and preview receive no OpenCode sidecar URL credential or bearer secret. Main authenticates only to the exact app-owned child and keeps that credential in its private process boundary. Never put credentials in a static bundle, URL query, cookie, log, export, or preview. Provider credentials remain in the existing runtime's storage and are not returned to UI. A single-user local app does not solve same-device malware or OS privilege risks.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:104:모든 파일 저장은 읽은 내용의 digest/mtime/identity를 version으로 받아 현재 version과 비교한 뒤 쓰며, 외부 변경은 충돌로 보존한다. Git stage/unstage/restore/commit/branch는 정확한 workspace Git root·HEAD·index 상태를 재확인한다. restore와 물리 삭제는 preview token에 포함된 경로·상태 digest가 달라지면 재확인을 요구한다. 원본 저장소 루트, 홈/파일시스템 루트, 설정된 작업 루트 자체와 그 상위, 중첩 등록 경로, 다른 session이 사용하는 경로를 물리 삭제에서 막는다. 무결성이 불확실할 때 앱은 성공으로 확정하지 않는다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:114:정책 변경은 `requested → admitting_paused → draining → applied → effective`다. 축소 시 새 도구 admission을 먼저 막고 pending 승인은 무효화 또는 새 revision으로 재검토한다. 활성 호출의 실제 종료를 확인하거나 해당 호출의 완료까지 `draining`을 유지한다. UI의 '전환 중'은 requested/admitting_paused/draining의 표시 범주이며 별도 wire 상태가 아니다. 즉시 중단 불가능한 호출을 종료했다고 표시하지 않는다. native session permission update가 성공해도 자식·MCP·직접 도구에 동일 revision이 적용됐다는 증거가 없으면 `effective`로 승격하지 않는다. 실패 시 이전 유효 정책을 유지하되, 축소 요청 뒤 정책이 불확실한 경우 새 위험 호출은 계속 막는다. 확대는 사용자에게 범위·적용 시점을 확인한 뒤 새 revision을 적용하며 기존 자식에 자동 전파하지 않는다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:126:| F-03 / AC-03 | worktree.remove는 기록된 strategy 사용; session delete는 child를 포함 | 등록 해제·대화 삭제·물리 삭제를 서로 다른 operation으로 구현. 마지막 경로/dirty/활성 소유 재검사, branch 보존 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:127:| F-04 / AC-04 | session list/create/update/delete/fork | 앱 title·pinned·archived·draft·unread·workspace 매핑; 최소 두 병렬 session과 재시작 복구 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:128:| F-05 / AC-05 | session message/interrupt/fork, message/context 조회 | 첨부·참조 검증, 대기 메시지, 재시도는 새 run/branch. 이전 effect 자동 재실행 금지 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:129:| F-06 / AC-06 | agent/model list, session agent/model 전환, context 조회 | requested/default/observed와 다음 적용 경계 기록; 미지원 effort 차단 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:130:| F-07 / AC-07 | session.fork는 history 복사; child 관련 native 동작은 버전 확인 | fresh child는 빈 native session + 명시적 payload/parent mapping. 두 child 병렬·개별 실패·취소·결과 회수 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:131:| F-08 / AC-08 | 도구는 session 실행에 포함; plugin tools/RPC 확장점 | schema 검증된 직접 실행 adapter 또는 검증된 RPC. 일반 도구 카드 fallback과 별도 permission 게이트 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:132:| F-09 / AC-09 | session.update permissions, pending/list/reply/remove saved permission | revision 전환·재평가·중복/만료 CAS, native 실제 강제·child 전파 검증 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:136:| F-13 / AC-13 | command.list, session.command, skill.list | 출처별 registry, schema/인자·busy 확인, 앱 명령 라우팅. TUI 전용 명령은 미지원 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:138:| F-15 / AC-15 | session message·tool 결과 | 앱 plan version/approval/checklist/review/evidence; 자기 보고와 검증 결과 분리 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:139:| F-16 / AC-16 | session statistics/context와 event stream | 로컬 event 일지, 제공/추정/미제공 usage, 설정 비교, 합성 학습 답·근거 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:140:| F-17 / AC-17 | session export/import는 대화 기록용; native event는 live-only | snapshot 재조회·gap, 앱 범위 export/import·retention·삭제, 불확실 effect 재실행 금지 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:147:`delete-check`는 `{workspaceId, canonicalPath, pathIdentity, sourceKind, ownerStrategy, dirtyPaths, untrackedPaths, activeSessions, activeChildren, terminals, servers, nestedProjects, branchPolicy, checkRevision}`을 반환한다. UI 확인은 이 목록·절대 경로·강제 여부를 받지만 실행 허가는 아니다. `delete`는 동일 checkRevision, 별도 destructive confirmation, 비강제 기본값으로 시작하고 마지막 identity·dirty·소유를 재검사한다. 원본 repo/보호 경로, 활성 실행·다른 session, 중첩 경로는 거절한다. force는 dirty/untracked 손실 목록과 경로 재확인이 있어야 한다. 기록된 strategy 제거 실패 뒤 임의 `rm -rf`로 가지 않는다. 일반 import 폴더의 실제 제거도 별도 확인한 adapter가 책임진다. 취소·등록 해제·기록 삭제는 파일 제거를 호출하지 않는다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:151:assistant-ui는 thread/composer/stream/render를 맡고, app projection이 `sessionId`, `runId`, message/part ID, queued input, interrupt state를 공급한다. 공식 OpenCode runtime의 [현재 quickstart](https://www.assistant-ui.com/docs/runtimes/opencode/quickstart)는 구세대 패키지 예시이므로 새 v2에 곧바로 맞는다고 보지 않는다. 불일치 시 [ExternalStoreRuntime](https://www.assistant-ui.com/docs/runtimes/custom/external-store)로 app projection을 연결한다. 모델 실행은 OpenCode 하나만 소유한다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:163:자동화 `Job`은 `{jobId, workspaceId, schedule, timezone, policyRevision, paused, nextDueAt, lastRunId?}`다. bridge가 살아 있는 동안만 scheduler가 실행한다는 잠정 계약이며 OS 상주 보장은 패키징 선택까지 보류한다. 시작 직전 경로·policy·자격 상태를 재검사한다. bridge가 꺼진 구간의 due는 `missed`로 남기고 소급 실행하지 않는다. 동일 due slot은 단일 operation key로 묶으며 crash 후 effect unknown을 재실행하지 않는다. 알림은 job/session ID와 상태만 표시하고 민감 본문은 넣지 않는다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:167:앱 export는 먼저 manifest를 만든다: schema version, 앱/SDK 버전, 선택된 project/session/event/artifact 범위, 파일 원문 포함 여부, 마스킹된 필드, 예상 크기, 대상 경로와 외부 provider/MCP 보존 한계. 실제 아카이브에는 secret, provider credential, 환경 변수 원문, 임의 프로젝트 전체 디렉터리를 기본 포함하지 않는다. 완성 파일은 임시 경로에 만들고 checksum 검증 뒤 원자적으로 목적지로 옮긴다. export 성공은 대상 파일 재조회로 확인한다. native session export는 그 자체로 앱의 workspace·policy·일지를 보존하지 않으므로 별도 manifest와 매핑한다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:169:import는 미리보기 단계에서 schema·checksum·크기·경로 탈출·중복 native/app ID를 검사한다. 기존 프로젝트 경로를 임의로 덮어쓰지 않고 새 앱 ID와 provenance를 부여하며, 불러온 외부 경로는 존재·identity·trust를 다시 검사한다. native session import가 대화 기록용이라는 점을 표시하고 실행 중 process, 권한 승인, 과거 부작용을 복원했다고 주장하지 않는다. 부분 import 실패는 어떤 앱 객체가 생성됐는지 기록하고, 실행을 자동 시작하지 않는다. 보존 기간 만료 또는 앱 데이터 삭제는 앱 DB/객체 저장소와 외부 파일·provider·MCP 보존 범위를 구별한다. 기록 삭제는 프로젝트 파일 삭제와 다른 transaction이며 진행 중 실행·권한과 연결된 증거는 안전한 종료·범위 확인 뒤 제거한다.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:177:| S-01 host | The fixed app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` binary and version-matched `@opencode/client`: per-OS identity/readiness/auth, session/event recovery, failure, shutdown and child reaping on the exact process | If a required behavior fails, hold engine integration and return an evidence-backed change proposal; do not silently substitute embedded host/shared service/client behavior |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:182:| S-06 direct tools/commands | 도구 schema·직접 실행 경로와 command.list/session.command 인자·취소/충돌 확인 | 검증된 plugin RPC 또는 app action adapter; TUI 전용은 미노출 |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:184:| S-08 bridge/preview | In browser-test-only mode, test browser bootstrap/origin/host/WS/cookie behavior. In Electron mode, separately test main/preload sender and payload admission, sidecar credential non-disclosure, preview isolation, navigation and file path escape | Keep the mode boundary explicit; any failed host admission or preview isolation blocks the affected desktop capability and release |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:186:| S-10 platform | Verify Electron window/process lifecycle, native dialog, notification, close/restart and macOS/Windows behavior | Packaged Electron E2E and lifecycle evidence on both OSes; independent runs on actual macOS and Windows systems |
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:196:5. **일상 사용과 출시:** F-16/17/18 완성. export/import/retention, 학습 답·근거, 사용량 출처, 설정·접근성·알림, scheduler pause/missed. AC-01~18과 PRD의 7개 통합 시나리오를 실제 지원 환경에서 독립 검토 후 판정.
docs/engineering/workbench-architecture.md:200:Electron and app-owned OpenCode v2 `serve` sidecar are selected/confirmed, while exact package versions and compatibility, work root, data location/retention, native permission/worktree/tool extension remain unverified. S-01 validates the fixed binary/client pair without reopening the host type. Preserve the approved product scope while recording observations, alternatives, cost, and risk for each remaining decision. Cross-review this document with UX/verification/operations; it is not implementation authority until current independent `design_spec_reviewer` and architecture reviews pass and the exact integrated set is explicitly approved. Static document review does not prove OS-level path protection, real permission enforcement, SDK compatibility, or preview isolation.

